ey "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160700}] :question/id #uuid "615b6ed0-1120-5f2d-a6c0-2c676050f1ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-90846" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f: R → R$ which is given by $f(x) = 3^{x}$?\n\n1. The range of $f$ is $(0, ∞)$\n2. $∀y ∈ R$, $∃x ∈ R$ such that $f(x) = y$\n3. $f$ maps $R$ **into** $R$"}]}
